## Stopping Logic

```typescript
const MAX_QUESTIONS = 7;
const RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD = 0.70;

function shouldStop(session: AnonymousSession): boolean {
  if (session.askedIds.length >= MAX_QUESTIONS) return true;
  return isResolved(session.distribution, RESOLUTION_THRESHOLD);
}
```

Educational inserts do NOT increment `askedIds.length`.

---

## Jargon Exception for Educational Inserts

The global jargon rule ("zero crypto terms to user") has one exception:
**Educational inserts intentionally introduce and define the terms USDC, ARC, and USYC.**

The rule still applies everywhere else (mandate card, strategy, dashboard, execution, notifications).

Within educational inserts, use the term + immediately define it in plain language:
> "USDC is a digital dollar — 1 USDC = exactly $1, always."
> "ARC is a fast financial network built by the creators of USDC."
> "USYC is backed by US government bonds — the safest investment in the world."

Never use DeFi, protocol, gas, staking, yield, APY, seed phrase, wallet, or blockchain in educational inserts.
